{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And this for Judah</b> — similarly, he said concerning Judah that he shall live and not die, and he added further for him, \"Hear, O YHWH, the voice of Judah\" — this is the opinion of Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Deuteronomy 33:7). But this is not correct according to our interpretation, for Judah is not in this lot such that one would pray for him in this manner, just as he did not mention such a thing for the rest of the tribes. Rather, it is according to its plain sense: \"and this is the blessing that belongs to Judah.\" And by way of truth, He singled out this attribute for Judah because to them belongs warfare, and from him is the kingship forever, and it is the help from his foes. And it is the secret of what is written, for it says (II Samuel 1:18), \"to teach the children of Judah the bow; behold, it is written in the Book of Jashar\" — for it is the bow that appears in the cloud, of which it is said concerning it (Genesis 9:17), \"this is the sign of the covenant.\"" "<b>Hear, O YHWH, the voice of Judah</b> — may He pray for him when he goes out to war, for he goes up first, and he is the leader from among them who wages war against the enemies of Israel, as Jacob said (Genesis 49:8), \"Your hand shall be on the neck of your enemies.\"" "<b>And to his people You shall bring him</b> — that he shall return in peace. <b>His hands shall contend for him</b> (ידיו רב לו) — let his hands be much for him, that he should not need the help of another besides the help of HaShem, who answers him in his prayer, according to all that is written in the words of Onkelos (Onkelos on Deuteronomy 33:7), and so is the opinion of the commentators. In my opinion, it further alludes to his first war against the Canaanite, of which HaShem said, \"Judah shall go up first\" (Judges 1:2), and it says <b>ידיו רב</b>, that he shall take from his foes and conquer from them lands more numerous than what is fitting for him in his inheritance — this alludes that he shall bequeath part of his inheritance to Simeon his brother, as it is said (Joshua 19:9), \"From the territory of the children of Judah was the inheritance of the children of Simeon, for the portion of the children of Judah was too much for them, and the children of Simeon inherited within their inheritance.\" And behold, he mentioned Simeon in an allusion together with Judah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The verse cited as '(א יח)' is II Samuel 1:18; Ramban cites it by its opening word א and chapter number."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:57.049000612Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}